  "body": "If you're looking for a 4-5 bedroom weatherboard home, drenched in all-day sun and only a 4min drive to St Heliers Village, come check out this very quiet family-friendly 1950's home, located well off the road. It offers open-plan living at its best with good separation downstairs for teenagers or extended family (and your own entranceway). The kitchen, dining and living room are designed for entertaining, and the newly sanded natural wooden floors create a relaxed atmosphere. Large floor-to-ceiling sliding doors open the home up to the north-facing patio, BBQ area and fully fenced in-ground pool complex. Your well-established tropical garden welcomes you home, and you will love summer nights watching the sun go down as you relax outside under the covered patio.  Internal access garaging, four off-street parks and multiple living areas means there is space for everyone. With so much more to see, viewing is essential.  Private, sunny and secure, you're going to love coming home. \r\n\r\n* 4.25kWh Solar System - $1,300 in electricity savings (2025)\r\n\r\n* Freehold\r\n\r\n* Land: 1,420sqm (more or less)\r\n\r\n* Floor area: 304sqm (approx.)\r\n\r\n* CV: $3,675,000 (2024)\r\n\r\n* Rates: $10,576.25\r\n\r\n* School zones: St Heliers School, St Ignatius Catholic School, Glendowie College, Baradene College\r\n\r\n* Rental Appraisal: $2,000 - $2,500\r\n\r\n* Zone: Residential - Mixed Housing Urban\r\n\r\nPlease call Jayne Kiely 021 352 007 or Amy Robertson 0274 820 100\r\n\r\nWe work with all agencies. Conjunctions are welcome.",
